        [SHIP'S LOGBOOK*];
        [Day 24:   Still looking for the miser's treasure.];
        [\x09\x09\x09   Fair wind and weather all day. The men are as excited as ever.];
        [\x09\x09\x09   Plundered a passing ship, appropriated some gold and wine.];
        [\x09\x09\x09   Lost one man in the fight.];
        [Day 31:   Very stormy weather and worse at night.];
        [\x09\x09\x09   No encounter.];
        [Day 32:   Uneventful except for repairs from last night's storm.];
        [Day 40:\x09This hideout is not easy to find. The men are becoming nervous.];
        [Day 41:\x09Ice filling the horizon! Temperature hath dropped.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09We are freezing. The men complain they have never seen];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09such weather this time of the year.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09Burning more and more oil to stay warm. Our provisions are];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09diminishing rapidly.];
        [Day 45:   Strange how ice magnifies all.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09Leaden sky is upon us. On the word of a pirate, we will];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09pierce through this as a sword through soft bellies!];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09A day of dead calm.];
        [Day 54:\x09Was forced to hang a brace of men who stole some food from the cook.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09The weather combined with our disappointing search for the];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09miser's base hath created an unbearable atmosphere.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09Ice is surrounding us and it feels as though we are imprisoned in];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09this place.];
        [Day 55:\x09We had a storm last night. Two men were found frozen on];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09the quarter-deck. One man missing. He most likely went overboard due];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09to the dense and damp fog, in that cold, inky black night.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09This treasure hunt is costing us too many men, and might];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09cost us even more...];
        [Day 56:\x09We are wedged in by an icefloe. Food is running low.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09Frozen land all around us, the ship is trapped.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09And so are we.];
        [Day 57\x09\x09Much arguing about rations.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09We are down to our last portion. We are but a few survivors,];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09bundled in our rags. The terror of the seas, HA!];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09We would not scare a mouse these days.];
        [Day 58:   Finishing each other is what we have been doing for];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09the last twenty-four hours. Such a waste! 'Tis only the];
        [ \x09\x09\x09two of us now and a portion of food, a single portion of food.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09Yet I shall not give in!];
    }
    if (v0 = 121) {
        [JOURNAL~~*];
        [Day 17 -- Everyone is overjoyed that we have actually ];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09reached the northern marches, including myself.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09I look forward to setting camp and finding treasure!*];
        [Day 22 -- We were forced to kill a pair of wolves near the encampment.];
        [Day 28 -- The men are upset that no gold hath been found...];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09However, I remain confident of our venture.*];
        [Day 40 -- Finding more wolves than gold.];
        [Day 41 -- Gold. At last!];
        [Day 45 -- Women and children are finding gold nuggets.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09How exciting! This is fabulous!];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09'Tis finally paying.*];
        [Day 69 -- More have been eaten alive.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09Wolves. More wolves.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09Men behaving like wolves. Worse than wolves.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09They are after our gold.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09For them, life is suddenly worthless.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09How could they value a nugget more than its];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09true worth?*];
        [Day 108 -- No one can be trusted.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09Who will be the next target?];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09Hopefully, I will survive and my gold will not];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09be stolen.*];
        [Day 121 -- Something horrible happened to Hamlin.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09He was found with his throat slit and, ];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09of course, his gold was missing.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09This worthless gold that he hath];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09painstakingly gathered killed him.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09So, this is what it hath come to...];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09Goldthirsty and bloodthirsty bastards.*];
        [Day 127 -- I have finally found a vein of gold, from whence];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09I retrieved a small quantity with];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09my pick.*];
        [Day 148-149 --  I lay awake on my bedroll all night ];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09until dawn, cannot seem to be able to sleep.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09Too many angry thoughts disturbing my mind.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09At daybreak, I rose in a state of exhaustion.*];
        [Day 167 -- More men are fighting amongst themselves.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09I am so weary.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09Is this what I wanted?];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09The encampment is split into factions.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09Now, I will cease writing and rest by the];
        [\x09\x09\x09   fire, gathering much needed strength for];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09tomorrow.*];
        [Day 183 -- Draygan betrayed us. Who would have thought it?];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09 I think bitterly of his treachery.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09 The ship is burnt. We are doomed.];
        [\x09\x09\x09\x09 The howling is getting closer...];
